+## Capture and verification
+
+Host emission goldens (`chromium_149_macos_*_client_hello.hex`) are raw TLS
+ClientHello handshake bodies captured from the Chromium 149.0.7827.114
+production SSLClientSocket path with Persona seed `0x42…` and generation 7
+(default) / 8 (ML-DSA). Regression tests recreate the same feature state, seed,
+and generation and compare parsed protocol fields after GREASE normalization.
+
+Independent **Chrome-for-Testing 149.0.7827.115** captures (not Persona-steered)
+are stored under `reference/`:
+
+- `reference/chromium_149_macos_cft_default_client_hello.hex` — native macOS arm64
+- `reference/chromium_149_linux64_default_client_hello.hex` — Linux x86_64 via
+  Docker `linux/amd64` (QEMU) headless Chrome
+
+Parsed comparison (GREASE stripped): **ciphers, signature algorithms, supported
+versions, supported groups, and ALPN are identical** across those CFT macOS and
+Linux captures. Extension order differs and is intentionally seed-steered on the
+Nitrous host. Windows x64 Chrome-for-Testing was downloaded for archival; native
+Windows execution was not available on the capture host, so Windows identity
+shares the verified Chrome 149 desktop network cohort.
 
